lso been very many  heart-warming moments and since  dad passed away various accolades and  recognitions that have been bestowed  upon him  and has been mentioned of that in the  earlier presentations in particular  around broome with school  and social housing schemes in timperley  um  that would be really really honored with  all of those so it is  it's a really touching moment for myself  for hazel and for my sister susan  and for all of our family and a great  honour to receive  on behalf of my late father the honorary  alderman of the borough  and thank you very much and we really  appreciate if you said this evening  thank you very much neil for those words  on behalf of the council  i'd like to thank you for your words  this evening  and say that i am honored to have  chaired our meeting this evening  where we have paid tribute and  recognized the great achievements  of both former councillors jane bohr and  ray baraka mbe  as truly outstanding servants of our  borough  that then concludes this meeting i would  like to thank all the members and guests  for your attendance  we will stop the broadcast of this  meeting at this point but i would ask  members not to leave  so that we can start our scheduled  council meeting shortly  you may wish to mute and turn your  cameras off whilst we wait to start the  next meeting  thank you why not
 

